<title>RUSSIA: Russia sets bond coupons at 40.05 pct.</title>
<headline>Russia sets bond coupons at 40.05 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian finance ministry set a 40.05 percent coupon on OFZ interest-bearing government bonds series 24003 and 24004 payable in February, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Series 24003</p>
<p>    Maturity date    Feb 26, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor		486 days</p>
<p>    Coupon number    rbls volume	 pct	payment date</p>
<p>    Fifth		145,799	    58.48     Nov 27, 1996</p>
<p>    Sixth		 99,851	    40.05     Feb 26, 1997</p>
<p>Series 24004</p>
<p>    Maturity date    May 28, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor		553 days</p>
<p>    Fourth	     145,799	    58.48     Nov 27, 1996</p>
<p>    Fifth		 99,851	    40.05     Feb 26, 1997</p>
<p>--Anna Smirnova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
